  "id": "COMPOUND:30233 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is implicated in the inhibition of Caspase-5, a key enzyme in the extrinsic apoptosis pathway. This inhibition is mediated through a series of molecular interactions, with Caspase-5 being a target of multiple metabolites, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol. These metabolites are themselves targets of SNB-78, suggesting a complex, multi-tiered mechanism of action. The evidence supports a potential pathway where Angoroside-C modulates Caspase-5 activity, which in turn affects the downstream activity of SNB-78. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically linked relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Angoroside-C and SNB-78 remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets along this pathway underscores the importance of Caspase-5 in mediating the effects of Angoroside-C, and suggests that SNB-78 may play a role in amplifying or regulating this process.",
